BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.77 Tm (The most expensive firsthand case comes from Kurtis Hanni's Bison CFO engagement. The client was taking 200 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.55 Tm (from ordering inventory to selling it, 185 of them on a boat from overseas, with receivables stuck above 30 days and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 303.32 Tm (zero payable days because the supplier demanded payment at commitment [0WBeNhRVKHY @ 00:07:14]. That) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.10 Tm (stacked into a 230-day cash conversion cycle, roughly 11 months to get cash flow positive on a first order, and 235,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.87 Tm (dollars paid out before a single dollar came back [0WBeNhRVKHY @ 00:09:07]. The owner kept getting hit with tax) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.65 Tm (payments and felt like they were drowning inside a growing business that was eating all its cash. The fix was a supplier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 242.42 Tm (conversation: a different route cut shipping from 185 to 15 days, the new supplier did not demand payment until goods) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.20 Tm (landed in the warehouse, and follow-up systems pulled receivables from about 35 days to 20 over six months, landing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.97 Tm (the cycle at 45 days and the cash requirement at 67,000 dollars [0WBeNhRVKHY @ 00:11:29]. LedgerGurus reports) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 196.75 Tm (the same trap across its client base, regularly seeing brands holding 180 to 240 days of inventory and warning that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.52 Tm (accrual books can show profits while the cash sits somewhere between the factory and the customer [F-Y1cubdesE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 166.30 Tm (00:05:12].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.07 Tm (Growth itself is the trap several practitioners keep hitting. LedgerGurus watches owners sign a big wholesaler on net 60) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.85 Tm (terms, book a huge purchase order as revenue, and then sit without the cash while also pre-building a pile of inventory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 120.62 Tm (to push into that channel [F-Y1cubdesE @ 00:06:05]. A Simple Model's pool float seller made 10 million dollars of) Tj ET
