BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.87 Tm (disapproval [UcU7Ishu1lY @ 00:04:19]. Austin at Grow My Ads names the aggressive versions of the same play as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 433.65 Tm (suspension triggers: price baiting, checkout hacks and fake sale prices [hY8ZBC3A4uQ @ 00:03:19]. His alternative to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 418.42 Tm (faking a discount is honest price positioning, because in his words price will rule all, and a competitor 20% cheaper) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 403.20 Tm (beats the best feed. Wixpa adds the trap that catches new Shopify stores: a perfect product feed does not guarantee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 387.97 Tm (product approval. Contact, refund, shipping, privacy and terms pages are still required, along with visible business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 372.75 Tm (details, and suspensions remain possible even after a clean app setup [RHJvGN_6sf0 @ 00:04:47]. The rule across all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 357.52 Tm (four is simple. Edit prices only where the store gets them, mirror them exactly, and treat every sale price as a live claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 342.30 Tm (that Google checks daily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 327.07 Tm (History destruction is the quiet killer. KeyCommerce warns never to change an ID or SKU, because doing so would) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.85 Tm (create a new product for Google. They report performance dropping after IDs were changed [S1NhYxaPnic @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 296.62 Tm (00:06:21]. The same video flags a second trap. If a feed app such as Semrush or DataFeedWatch runs the catalog,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 281.40 Tm (manual Merchant Center edits get overridden on the next sync, so all work belongs in the app. Wixpa calls the product) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 266.17 Tm (ID format the migration trap. A new account keeps the default format, but a store switching apps must keep its previous) Tj ET
