BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 461.77 Tm (The costliest firsthand failures come from trusting platform numbers. Adam Callinan describes a $500k loss over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 446.55 Tm (roughly 16 months driven by overlapping 30-day attribution windows. The damage was compounded when iOS 14.5) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 431.32 Tm (blocked pixels on a traffic base that was about 80% iPhone [VCXWZQgbKXw @ 00:28:33]. The fix Callinan adopted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 416.10 Tm (was MER, or global ROAS, plus a DTC ROAS that folds in Amazon, used as a baseline rather than a scoreboard.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 400.87 Tm (Callinan pairs that with a breakeven ROAS curve derived from fixed costs and variable margin, because ad budgets) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 385.65 Tm (without a mathematical framework are simply gambling [VCXWZQgbKXw @ 00:23:59]. Leading Social reaches the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 370.42 Tm (same conclusion from the agency side. MER divides total revenue by total marketing, including agency and content) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 355.20 Tm (costs, which removes the channel bias where Meta can look strong while the business overall is under pressure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 339.97 Tm ([KpmUvCBEKK4 @ 00:02:48]. Paul Waddy adds the hidden ceiling behind rising spend: more budget mostly raises) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 324.75 Tm (frequency from one to five, showing the same ad to the same people without opening new demand [7v_KO8bj_G0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 309.52 Tm (00:26:38]. Callinan's working rule is to chart the contribution-profit trend line and judge strategy by whether it climbs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 294.30 Tm (regardless of what any dashboard claims about individual campaigns that month.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 279.07 Tm (Cash and cost structure kill brands that look healthy on revenue. Paul Waddy calls inventory probably the number one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 263.85 Tm (reason brands go insolvent. Waddy prescribes about three months of stock cover, replenishment at 30 days, and four) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 248.62 Tm (inventory turns a year. Supplier terms such as no deposit and payment 30 days after arrival turn months two and three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 233.40 Tm (into accumulated cash [7v_KO8bj_G0 @ 00:34:39]. Adam Callinan's firsthand reversal came from fixed costs: in 2019) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 218.17 Tm (the business gave back all of the profit earned in 2018. That loss drove a rule of keeping fixed costs under 20% of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 202.95 Tm (revenue and chasing more contribution profit with fewer fixed expenses [VCXWZQgbKXw @ 00:41:34]. Bloom) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 187.72 Tm (Analytics shows how thin the margin for error is. An $82 new-customer AOV minus $50 of variable costs leaves $32) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 172.50 Tm (of gross unit profit, and a $50 CAC drives first-order contribution to minus $18. Repeat purchases only reach) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 157.27 Tm (breakeven around day 56, a close call against the 60-day target [IlWyYcfaKpg @ 00:01:38]. The trap is that CAC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 142.05 Tm (keeps climbing while gross profit stays flat, so payback quietly stretches past the window that justified spending more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 126.82 Tm ([IlWyYcfaKpg @ 00:02:31]. Revenue growth alone hides every one of these leaks until the bank balance says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 111.60 Tm (otherwise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 96.37 Tm (Operational breakage and strategic drift form the third failure cluster. Justin Lalonde puts it bluntly: when you scale) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 81.15 Tm (fast, operations and supply chain break, which is why owners near $1M often push for better rather than more) Tj ET
